{
 "round": "S3-R13",
 "what_this_is": "The FC Special deferred-load implementation (operator decision, R13 S1), measured in real headless Chrome over a populated fixture world; plus the SKU Regional cold-entry matrix (S9).",
 "instrument": "assets/tests/_s3r11-interaction-runner.js, extended for R13 with: the Special builder deferred boundaries (a SKU typed into a row, a group build, an existing event picked), a stall that can name a TABLE rather than only an action, and the S9 cold-entry matrix.",
 "harness_faults_found_and_fixed": [
  "THE getTable FIXTURE ANSWERED THE WRONG ENVELOPE, AND HAD SINCE R11. _kmGetTableOnce_ returns json.data.rows; the fixture answered { data: { <table>: rows } }, so EVERY getTable in this harness resolved to [] - a successful read of an empty table. Request counts were unaffected, which is why R11 and R12 request/round findings stand: a count is a property of control flow, not of the payload. What could never be exercised was anything reading the broad cache ROWS - which is exactly what this round defers. Left unfixed, every R13 assertion would have passed over an empty world.",
  "THE EVENT FIXTURE WAS OUT OF SCOPE FOR THE BUILDER DEFAULTS. R12 rows were US/Amazon/this-year and used target_year / start_date / forecast_qty, while normalizeFcSpecialEventRecord reads year / event_start_date / fc_qty and _evtExistingEvents_ filters on raw.year. The builder opens on the FIRST country option and on fcTargetYear (NEXT year), so every row was filtered out. R12 recorded options:1, unreadable:false and read that as the picker being readable - which was true, and was not the question. The fixture now covers every scope the builder can open on, in both years it can default to.",
  "campaigns and campaign_sku_lines were literally [] in the fixture, which would have made THE DEFERRED TABLE LOADED and THE DEFERRED TABLE IS EMPTY the same observation."
 ],
 "what_is_authoritative": [
  "Request counts, read ROUNDS, and which broad-cache getters each path calls. Identical at serverMs 0 and 400, which is what makes them properties of the control flow.",
  "DOM outcomes: the price cell state (pending vs missing vs ok), whether a subsection refusal is scoped, whether the rest of the builder is still rendered, whether a hydrate produced a discount."
 ],
 "what_is_not": [
  "pollMs - Chrome virtual time, as recorded in the R11 and R12 evidence. Production milliseconds remain operator-owned. The operator figures carried into this round (~6s Regular, ~37s Special) are approximate and are NOT converted into benchmarks."
 ],
 "special_initial_path": {
  "SPECIAL_INITIAL_REQUEST_COUNT_PRE": 4,
  "SPECIAL_INITIAL_REQUEST_COUNT_POST": 2,
  "SPECIAL_INITIAL_ROUNDS_PRE": 2,
  "SPECIAL_INITIAL_ROUNDS_POST": 1,
  "SPECIAL_INITIAL_TABLES_POST": [
   "sku_details",
   "marketplace_skus",
   "campaigns"
  ],
  "SPECIAL_INITIAL_SLICE_POST": "fcSummary.workspace.get slice=events",
  "note": "PRE is R12 measured and recorded in docs/evidence/s3-r12-fc-cold-path/measurements.json. Both figures are taken in the same harness after a Regular open has warmed sku_details and marketplace_skus. The DECLARED cold set moves from 5 tables (3 rounds at a read pool of 2) to 3 tables (2 rounds) for a session that goes straight to Special."
 },
